data: {"v": {"type": "message", "data": {"id": "8868e758-d43b-4190-bf3f-9bc898d68de8", "author": {"role": "assistant", "name": null, "metadata": {"sonicberry_model_id": "current_gpt5_1_reasoning_paid", "real_author": "tool:web", "source": "sonic_tool"}}, "create_time": 1775327510.423188, "update_time": null, "content": {"content_type": "text", "parts": ["\ue200image_group\ue202{\"layout\":\"bento\",\"aspect_ratio\":\"1:1\",\"query\":[\"GitHub logo\",\"GitHub website UI repository\",\"GitHub Copilot interface\",\"GitHub Octocat mascot\",\"GitHub office San Francisco\"],\"num_per_query\":1}\ue201  \n\n## GitHub  \n\nGitHub is a cloud-based code hosting and collaboration platform built around the \ue200entity\ue202[\"company\",\"Git\",\"distributed version control system\"]\ue201 ecosystem. It lets developers store, version, review, and ship software together and is operated by GitHub, Inc., a subsidiary of \ue200entity\ue202[\"company\",\"Microsoft\",\"technology company\"]\ue201. As of 2025 it serves over 150 million developers and 420+ million repositories, making it the world\u2019s largest source code host. \ue200cite\ue202turn0search0\ue202turn0search1\ue201  \n\n### Key facts  \n\n- **Type:** Subsidiary software company (developer platform, code hosting) \ue200cite\ue202turn0search0\ue201  \n- **Founded:** 2008; headquarters in San Francisco, USA \ue200cite\ue202turn0search0\ue201  \n- **Founders:** Tom Preston-Werner, Chris Wanstrath, P. J. Hyett, Scott Chacon \ue200cite\ue202turn0search0\ue201  \n- **Parent company:** Microsoft (acquired in 2018 for $7.5B) \ue200cite\ue202turn0search0\ue201  \n- **Scale:** 150M+ users, 420M+ repositories (largest code host) \ue200cite\ue202turn0search0\ue202turn0search1\ue201  \n\n### What GitHub actually does  \n\nGitHub provides Git-based version control with an easy web UI plus collaboration tools: pull requests, code review, issues, project boards, discussions, and wikis. Repositories can be public or private, letting individuals, open-source communities, and enterprises manage everything from tiny scripts to massive monorepos. \ue200cite\ue202turn0search0\ue202turn0search3\ue201  \n\nIt also offers integrated CI/CD via GitHub Actions, security scanning (Dependabot, secret scanning, code scanning), and package registries so teams can build, test, and release software from a single platform. \ue200cite\ue202turn0search0\ue201  \n\n### AI and developer experience  \n\nGitHub builds AI tools like GitHub Copilot and GitHub Copilot Enterprise, which use large language models to suggest code, explain snippets, generate tests, and help with documentation directly in the editor and on the platform. This positions GitHub not just as storage for code, but as an active coding assistant and automation hub. \ue200cite\ue202turn0search0\ue202turn0search2\ue201  \n\n### Business model and customers  \n\nGitHub runs a freemium SaaS model: free tiers for individuals and open source, plus paid plans (GitHub Pro, Team, and Enterprise) with advanced security, compliance, and management features. It\u2019s widely used by solo developers, open-source projects, startups, and large enterprises across many industries. \ue200cite\ue202turn0search0\ue202turn0search1\ue201  \n\n### Governance, history, and ownership  \n\nCreated in 2007\u20132008 as a startup focused on making Git easier to use, GitHub grew rapidly, surpassing older code hosts like SourceForge and Google Code by the early 2010s. \ue200cite\ue202turn0search0\ue201 In 2018 it was acquired by Microsoft but continues to operate with its own brand and roadmap, while integrating deeply with the broader Microsoft developer ecosystem (for example, Visual Studio Code and Azure). \ue200cite\ue202turn0search0\ue201"]}, "status": "finished_successfully", "end_turn": true, "weight": 1.0, "metadata": {"content_references": [{"matched_text": "\ue200image_group\ue202{\"layout\":\"bento\",\"aspect_ratio\":\"1:1\",\"query\":[\"GitHub logo\",\"GitHub website UI r